course: dictionary
lesson: 1054
title: Bots
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A bot is a computer program that does jobs by itself, without a person pressing every button. Many bots are made to pretend to be people. Context helps you check this: «The bot is patient.» A patient bot waits calmly, so a bot here is something that acts like a person.
explain: Read the words around a word for clues. «Bots tend to flatter; praise from a bot that has not seen your work tells you nothing.» The second part says the praise tells you nothing, so flatter must mean praising too much, even when it is not earned.
explain: Bot can also be short for robot. Swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. «When a bot invents a confident answer that is not true, people call it a "hallucination".» Here a bot is a computer program, because a robot does not invent answers on a screen.
fact: A bot is a computer program that does tasks by itself.
fact: Some bots pretend to be people, for example when they answer your messages.
fact: «Bot» is sometimes short for robot.
fact: «Hallucination» means a bot giving a confident answer that is not true.
fact: Some bots spread fake news or scams, so be careful online.
exercise: «A bot never gets impatient with repeated explanations.» What does this tell you about a bot? | *It does not get annoyed, even when you ask again | It only answers questions in the morning | It gets cross when you ask the same question twice | It never answers any questions at all
exercise: What is a bot? | A small furry animal that lives in a burrow | A password that keeps your account safe | *A computer program that does tasks by itself, often pretending to be a person | A teacher who marks homework on a screen
exercise: «When a bot invents a confident answer that is not true, people call it a "hallucination".» Find and copy the word for a confident answer that is not true. | flatter | *hallucination | patient | chatbot
test: What is a chatbot? | A robot that cooks dinner | *A bot you can talk to that answers your questions | A message sent by a friend | A card game played on a table
test: «Bots tend to flatter; praise from a bot that has not seen your work tells you nothing.» What does flatter mean? | *Praise too much, to please you | Tell you the truth about your work | Ignore your work completely | Copy your work exactly
exam: Ella says, «A bot is always a real person typing.» Is she right? | *No, a bot is a computer program that does tasks by itself | No, bots never send any messages | Yes, a bot is always a real person typing | Yes, bots are always robots with arms and legs
